{
  "meta": {
    "id": "t6_02",
    "tier": 6,
    "order_in_tier": 2,
    "title": "Sharp-Key Chromatic Voicing",
    "composer_source": "Romantic Prelude Study in F# Minor",
    "key": {
      "fifths": 3,
      "mode": "minor"
    },
    "time_signature": {
      "numerator": 4,
      "denominator": 4
    },
    "target_bpm": 68.0,
    "theory": {
      "summary": "Trains 3-sharp minor fluency (F#, C#, G# + E# leading tone) with Romantic inner voices and diminished-7th pivots.",
      "pattern_tip": "Read E#4 cleanly as the raised leading tone of F# minor (V7 = C#7), and spot G#dim7 bridging i to iv.",
      "technique_tip": "Keep the wrist supple when voicing chromatic inner lines against low F#2/C#2 pedal anchors.",
      "ballade_link": "Eliminates sharp-key and enharmonic reading hesitation during Chopin's middle-section A-major/F#-minor modulations.",
      "concept_title": "Sharp-Key Reading Fluency (F# Minor / E#) & Diminished Pivots",
      "concept_paragraphs": [
        "Reading three sharps (F#, C#, G#) in minor\u2014especially with the white-key enharmonic leading tone E# on C#7 (V6/5 = C#7/E#)\u2014often trips up learners accustomed to C or G minor. Knowing F# minor inside-out makes Chopin's sharp middle episodes feel natural.",
        "Listen closely to Bar 6's G#dim7 (iio7): symmetrical minor thirds pull tension tightly inward before expanding onto the F#m/C# (i6/4) -> C#7 -> F#m cadence."
      ],
      "form_map": [
        {
          "phrase_label": "Phrase A (Bars 1-4)",
          "role": "Expressive F#-minor opening tracing C#7/E# (V6/5) to Half Cadence C#."
        },
        {
          "phrase_label": "Phrase B (Bars 5-8)",
          "role": "Builds through Bm (iv) and G#dim7 (iio7) into a rich F#m/C# cadential 6/4."
        },
        {
          "phrase_label": "Phrase C (Bars 9-12)",
          "role": "Lifts briefly through A (III), D (VI), and E7 (VII7) before closing in F#m."
        }
      ],
      "practice_steps": [
        "1. Locate E# (= F key) immediately whenever you see C#7/E# in the harmony.",
        "2. Run Skeleton mode to map F#m -> Bm -> G#dim7 -> C#7 cleanly across the black keys.",
        "3. Keep wrists supple when voicing chromatic inner lines against low F#/C# anchors.",
        "4. Perform smoothly at 68 BPM with balanced Romantic singing tone."
      ],
      "audio_examples": [
        {
          "label": "Sharp-Key Leading Tone & Diminished Pivot",
          "caption": "F#m -> C#7/E# -> F#m -> Bm -> G#dim7 -> F#m/C# -> C#7 -> F#m",
          "chords": [
            "F#m",
            "C#7/E#",
            "Bm",
            "G#dim7",
            "F#m/C#",
            "C#7",
            "F#m"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "tempo_marking": "Andante con moto"
  },
